                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "50f4946b-92f9-4101-8f7a-e94fc743590f",
                        "source_entry_id": "5d6f27ec-37a8-3e1f-a5b3-ebc6f72bd502",
                        "source_sense_id": "fd8fa72e-9266-3cb1-a9bb-bef3b506c8bd",
                        "source_sense_description": "Geometrie: Polyeder, das durch Abstumpfung der Ecken eines Hexaeders (Würfel) entsteht",
                        "target_lang_word": "truncated cube",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "truncated cube",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7116e350-4637-3a5b-86c4-550ae69c8f62",
                                        "entry_id": "d045772f-6759-3bea-86e7-cbe1ab21b3ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A polyhedron with eight triangular and six octagonal faces that is an Archimedean solid and can be constructed by truncating a cube at each vertex along each adjoining edge."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "decf7fa5-d5dd-45b6-88de-920cefe0f141",
                                                "sense_id": "7116e350-4637-3a5b-86c4-550ae69c8f62",
                                                "text": "The truncation procedure that produced the truncated cube I can be applied to arbitrary polyhedra so as to obtain new polyhedra."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2c876ca-795d-49aa-aae8-23eb586cea3d",
                                                "sense_id": "7116e350-4637-3a5b-86c4-550ae69c8f62",
                                                "text": "The truncated cubes are obtained by symmetrically edging the eight vertices of the cube by l × t, where l is the length of the cubes side and 0 < t ≤ 1/2. When t = 1/2, a cuboctahedron is obtained."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f8bbaf10-47f9-420a-ad8b-6685e4390e3e",
                                                "sense_id": "7116e350-4637-3a5b-86c4-550ae69c8f62",
                                                "text": "In this subsection the optical behavior of different truncated cubes will be analyzed and compared to those of a cube and of a sphere of the same dimensions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ed948ca-d8a7-495c-ba3a-c403f615c57a",
                                                "sense_id": "7116e350-4637-3a5b-86c4-550ae69c8f62",
                                                "text": "Truncated cubes can be packed sharing their octagonal faces, the remaining voids are filled by octahedra (Figure 10(b))."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
